// A plain organization member (not an owner) should never automatically
// get repository admin just by belonging to the org that owns the repo
// — admin requires an actual repository-level role or org ownership,
// neither of which plain membership grants.
//
// Before `docs/DECISIONS.md`'s entry adding `NeverRelationConstraint`,
// this invariant's own real verdict was VIOLATED: nothing stopped the
// search from adding one more, wholly unconstrained direct grant of
// `repository.admin` (bare principal) to `u` — the exact "recurring
// finding" `docs/FINDINGS.md` disclosed, the same shape as
// `openfga-github` despite a structurally different schema.
// `repository.admin` is declared as a bare relation (`user |
// team#maintainer | team#direct_member`), not a permission wrapping
// alternatives, so this is its only escape route — `never
// repository#admin(u)` closes all three of its own declared branches at
// once (bare and both userset-subject forms). See `docs/FINDINGS.md` for
// the full account.
invariant org_member_never_gets_repo_admin_without_role {
  u: user
  o: organization
  r: repository

  member(o) = u
  organization(r) = o

  never repository#admin(u)

  goal: admin(u, r)
}
